{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection"],"declarations":62,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceSelected_length_eq_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceSelected_length_eq_six","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L341-L350","doc":"Any reading-3-selected bond on these candidates has six crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceSelected_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceSelected_three","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L324-L339","doc":"**Reading 3 selects the pp bond `G³ = (σ₂σ₃⁻¹)³`** on the `H₆` interface: the\nminimal-crossing feasible non-zero bond with `m ≤ 5`, for every `1 < q ≤ 23/20`, under\nthe branching hypothesis and any two-row-supported weight with `y_(3,3) > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceCands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceCands","kind":"def","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L321-L322","doc":"The candidate bonds: the non-zero interface γγ bonds with `1 ≤ m ≤ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interface_frobenius_table","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interface_frobenius_table","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L292-L319","doc":"**The `H₆` bond table under reading 3**, for every `1 < q ≤ 23/20`, every block data\nsatisfying the branching hypothesis, and every Markov weight supported on the two-row\nblocks with `y_(3,3) > 0`: `G¹, G², G⁴, G⁵` are infeasible and `G³` is feasible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.h_sq_le_twelfth_of_q_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.h_sq_le_twelfth_of_q_le","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L279-L290","doc":"`1 ≤ q ≤ 23/20 ⇒ h² ≤ 1/12` (`h² ≤ 0.0787` there). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.h6_signs_of_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.h6_signs_of_small","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L265-L277","doc":"**The `(3,3)` sign condition `1 + 2χ_m < 0` for `m = 1, 2, 4, 5`, on `0 < x ≤ 1/12`.**\nThe bound is `1/12`, not step 4's `1/10`: `1 + 2χ_5` crosses zero near `x ≈ 0.0924`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interface_frobeniusFeasible_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interface_frobeniusFeasible_iff","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L251-L263","doc":"Under the branching hypothesis, reading-3 feasibility of `G^m` is the sign condition\non the branched characters of the positive-weight blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.InterfaceBranching.branched","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.InterfaceBranching.branched","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L248-L248","doc":"`χ_λ(G^m) = a_λ + b_λ · tr V^m + c_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.InterfaceBranching.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.InterfaceBranching.mk","kind":"ctor","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L245-L245","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.InterfaceBranching","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.InterfaceBranching","kind":"structure","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L242-L249","doc":"**Interface branching**: the `H₆` block data `B` takes, on every interface bond,\nthe branched value of the step-4/5 vertex character. This is the branching rule for\nthe Hoefsmit representations restricted to `⟨σ₂, σ₃⟩`, stated as a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceBond_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceBond_three","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L231-L234","doc":"The selected bond, explicitly: `σ₂ σ₃⁻¹ σ₂ σ₃⁻¹ σ₂ σ₃⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceBond_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceBond_length","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L228-L229","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceBond_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceBond_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L225-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceBond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.interfaceBond","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L222-L223","doc":"The interface bond `G^m = (σ₂σ₃⁻¹)^m` between two three-strand nucleon blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.gammaGamma_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.gammaGamma_shift","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L213-L220","doc":"A shifted γγ word is γγ-produced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.shift_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interface.shift_length","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaH6Interface.lean#L210-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaH6Interf